Tech Consultancy Analysis Project:

Overview:
I completed this project as part of IBM data analyst certificate program. I assumed the role of an associate Data Analyst role for a made-up tech consultancy company. My task is to identify trends related to current and future technologies and programming languages with data provided to guide business decisions and identify patterns and trends.

Objectives:
Understand current and future technologies.
Understand current and future programming languages that respondants have mentioned.
Understand the respondants demographics. 
Understand which Integrated Web Development Environmnets are most popular among respondants.
Extract,Transform and Load data using Python libraries and SQL.
Extract data using APIs and Webscrapping.
Present findings to various stakeholders with business recommendations.

Tools Used:
Python(Numpy,Pandas,Seaborn, Matplotlib,Scikitlearn)
SQL(SQLite)
Google Looker Studio for dashboard
Powerpoint

Dataset used:

IBM Slack Survey Data
https://cf-courses-data.s3.us.cloud-object-storage.appdomain.cloud/VYPrOu0Vs3I0hKLLjiPGrA/survey-data-with-duplicate.csv

Initial Assessment:
Total number of rows were 65457.
The data possessed a lot of issues such as inconsistent data types eg. 'Age' column had text vlaues which were converted to nuneric values, 'Country' column had inconsistent values which were made consistent, some columns had null values which were replaced by their median such as the 'Age' column, duplicate values in 'MainBranch' were analyzed to understand if they were actually duplicates or if they were just shared responses. The compensation column 'ConvertedCompYearly' had one value skewing the result which was removed to get a better understanding of data. This column was also normalized and log transformed to reduce skewness.

Explanatory Data Analysis(EDA):

Finding 1: Most Common Work Arrangement
Most Respondants preferred working Hybrid about 34000 respondants.

Business Recommendation: Tech firm should consider adopting flexible hybrid work policies to attract and retain talent. Combining remote work with in-office collaboration can support employee satisfaction while maintaining teamwork and productivity.

Finding 2: Most Common Education Type
A Bachelors degree was fouund to be the most common education type among respondants

Business Recommendation:
The tech consultancy should consider a bachelor's degree as a common educational background when designing recruitment strategies and entry-level hiring requirements.

Finding 3: Frequently used Languages
Javascript was found to be the most populus langugage among respondants and HTML was found 2nd in place. Most respondants want to work with Python.

Business Recommendation:
The tech firm can introduce Python training courses for clients to increae their employment chances.

Finding 4: Database usage
PostgreSQL was found to be the most frequently used database in both future and current usage trends

Business Recommendation:
Our consultancy should prioritize PostgreSQL when recommending database technologies to clients. Since it remains popular among developers and is also highly preferred for future use, investing in PostgreSQL training and development skills can help organizations build and maintain reliable database solutions while accessing a strong talent pool.

Finding 5: Median Age
Median Age was found to be 32.7

Business Recommendation:
The median age of 32.7 suggests that the respondent population is relatively young and likely represents professionals in the early to middle stages of their careers. Our consultancy should consider this demographic when advising clients on talent development, recruitment, and employee retention strategies.

Conclusion:
The analysis provides valuable insights into current workforce preferences, education backgrounds, programming language trends, and database usage among respondents. The findings show a strong preference for hybrid work arrangements, with a bachelor's degree being the most common education level. JavaScript and HTML remain widely used, while Python stands out as a language many respondents want to learn or work with. PostgreSQL also maintains its position as the most popular database in both current and future usage trends.

With a median respondent age of 32.7, the results offer useful insight into the professional demographic represented in the survey. Based on these findings, our tech consultancy can help clients make more informed decisions by encouraging flexible work policies, supporting continuous learning and technical upskilling, and prioritizing relevant technologies such as Python and PostgreSQL.

Overall, these insights can help organizations adapt to changing workforce expectations, strengthen their technical capabilities, and make better-informed talent and technology decisions.

